From: "Atish (via Claude)" <atish9937@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:58:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Script keeps making the BUY recommendation; AI validates it

Correction to the previous pass: the script should still issue its own
BUY_CE/BUY_PE recommendation from the mechanical checklist + quality
score (daily_trend, intraday_trend, momentum, vwap_aligned,
nifty_aligned vs min_recommend_score), exactly as it always did. It is
not a neutral "candidate" that withholds a call.

What changed from the original is only the AI's role: instead of being
folded silently into the score (catalyst was always unscorable), AI now
explicitly VALIDATES the recommendation the script already made -
catalyst/news, cross-recommendation correlation, regime, and risk
sizing - via an "ai_validation" block on every BUY, and signs off
VALIDATED / VETOED / SIZE-DOWN rather than inventing the call itself.

- verdict is BUY_CE/BUY_PE again (was CANDIDATE_CE/CANDIDATE_PE)
- new CONFIG["min_recommend_score"] (4 of 5) drives the recommendation
- "ai_review" renamed "ai_validation"; batch block renamed
  AI_VALIDATION_BATCH / scan_recommendations
- signals_YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl restored (was candidates_YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl)
- docstring rewritten to describe recommend-then-validate, not
  collect-then-decide

